& [Implementation]
  + ScriptedStoppedRun binds a stopped IterativeReport exact successor registry optional failed request optional sanitized failed response optional fault reason provider-execution denial and compiled nonclaims
  + run_scripted_ready_stopped consumes a finite caller-supplied response script and admits at most one deterministic advancement per valid unique tool call
  + an exact tool-call cap stops at the latest admitted READY head without requesting or consuming another response
  + an exhausted response script records the deterministically reconstructed failed request but does not increment provider usage or invent response evidence
  + an invalid supplied response increments provider usage retains only its sanitized envelope and refuses advancement
  + terminal advancement is deliberately rejected because terminal-reflection-pending has a different identity from READY-stopped
  + resume_scripted_stopped returns a BoundSession only after the report wrapper prefix registry usage and failure evidence all validate

& [ReentryAndReplay]
  + the stopped report carries exactly one READY reentry handle and reentry_available true while all terminal and final-output fields remain absent
  + exact final-registry INSPECT must reproduce the reentry handle without changing the registry
  + provider-prefix replay reconstructs every admitted request assistant call matching tool result and the next failed request when present
  + resumed report segments may open at any nonzero READY sequence and must preserve predecessor identity and sequence continuity from that reentry point
  + sequence zero terminal openings stale handles contradictory cap evidence and inconsistent response accounting refuse

& [Equivalence]
  + the quota-one fixture stops after exactly one READY advancement with one provider call one tool call and a live successor registry
  + resuming that exact head and completing the remaining advancement reaches the same terminal outcome digest as uninterrupted quota-eight execution
  + a duplicate second call is counted as a supplied provider response but does not authorize a second tool advancement

& [HonestyAndSecurity]
  + READY stopped terminal pending and complete remain disjoint representations
  + missing input and invalid supplied input retain different evidence and usage
  + private reasoning is sanitized from retained response evidence
  + provider_execution_claimed remains false because every response is caller-supplied fixture material
  + exact state remains under host custody in the successor registry and never enters provider-shaped messages

& [Rollback]
  + the scripted_stopped module exports tests and nonzero segment-opening rule are additive
  + P0 through Slice4A behaviors remain independently reproducible

& [Deferred]
  + terminal-reflection-pending requires a separate Slice4C form and completion transition
  + HTTP provider process clock timeout persistence concurrency remote hidden-state effect FPGA and Minecraft behavior remain unimplemented and unactivated
